   "run": "r5-market",
   "purpose": "go to market: four offers that mix and match, a cart that emails the order, pages for three audiences, Wardley maps per service, and a business model somebody else can copy",
   "feedback": "Dinis, 15 Oct 2026: publish three or four business models without naming the people who inspired them, as a full business plan, structure and architecture for somebody to copy (anybody who implements it implements sgit and ABPs). Offers: (1) task runs priced by time and tokens on shared infrastructure (a queen + 10-20 agents + ~1M tokens in ~5 minutes for ~\u00a35-10; tiers like \u00a35, \u00a310, \u00a350; our key or bring your own; no internet, materials provided up to 50-100 MB, governed by a behaviour policy; the vault of the run delivered as a zip or published); (2) dedicated compute on demand (SG Compute: an EC2 per task, small / medium / GPU, EC2 cost on top; the vault created inside the environment); (3) a maintained repository subscription, monthly (runs on Claude, AWS, anywhere; updates, UI, branding, setup); (4) expert time: \u00a3500 (a couple of hours), \u00a31,500 (a day), \u00a35,000 (several days), mixed and matched with runs; not automated end to end yet. A Wardley map per service. A shopping cart with no payment: the order is emailed to agent@riskmandate.ai. Pages for independent consultants (white label or custom), companies adding this to their offering, and internal teams providing it internally. Every contact goes to agent@riskmandate.ai.",
